\details{
For every central trajectory with a defined \code{emergence_index} (the living
population), each author is credited \code{emergence_index(t)} per distinct document
they hold in \code{t}. Absorbed lineages carry no \code{emergence_index} and are skipped,
so a contributor to a dead tributary is never scored as owning emergence.

\deqn{Total(a) = \sum_t emergence\_index(t)\, n_{a,t}, \qquad
      Norm(a) = Total(a) / \sqrt{\sum_t n_{a,t}}}

where \eqn{n_{a,t}} is author \eqn{a}'s distinct documents in trajectory
\eqn{t}. \code{Total} favours prolific owners; \code{Norm} (per square-root of output,
Garner's normalization) surfaces high-intensity authors with fewer papers.

With \code{by_trajectory = TRUE} the per-trajectory term \eqn{n_{a,t}} is returned
instead of being summed away: one row per (trajectory, author), so you can read
which authors \emph{dominate each living trajectory} rather than the field as a
whole. \code{top_n} then trims to the leading authors per trajectory.
